''Testing `$funcChainTrigger`''
<br>
$cssDesc[With the following parameters:
<ol>

<li style="margin-bottom: 1em">str-type `_uniqueCountName`, (a pre-initiated variable)</li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 1em">num-type `_chainThreshold`,</li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 1em">str-type `_hookRevealed`,</li>
</ol>
]

<!--Best practice is to further place the macro into a temp var short hand-->
(set: _trigger to ($funcChainTrigger: "testAChain", 2, "TestA4Reveal"))

<br>

I've looked ($funcReveal: "high", "high") and ($funcReveal: "low", "low").

|high)[_trigger
<br>
She is not on the cupboards.
]

|low)[_trigger
<br>
She is not under the table either.
]

|TestA4Reveal)[
<br>
($funcReveal: "Where could she be?", "where")|where)[` `Ah, right here, by my side. _resetLink]
]